(5460259, 783086, 63499, '<td valign="top">I can''t say I''m surprised by the score, but I was hoping that this might score a 5. With my score so low, I was happily surprised to see the 9s and 10. I am curious if the low score is due to this being a pet in candid challenge or if it is missing something technically?</td>', 'I can''t say I''m surprised by the score, but I was hoping that this might score a 5. With my score so low, I was happily surprised to see the 9s and 10. I am curious if the low score is due to this being a pet in candid challenge or if it is missing something technically?', '2009-05-01 01:56:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460504, 784074, 57229, '<td valign="top">Darkness is necessary in a study of light. I''m wondering what could make this better and I''m not getting anywhere with the wondering. I think you could probably lose the strip of light in the foreground and crop to the shadow above it. He cuts a lovely figure and is showing proper respect for what he''s looking at, but if he were St Paul on the road to Damascus he would be looking at the source of the light instead of away from it. Where he''s looking it becomes more a study of the architecture than a study of the light and my wondering asks if a bit of the architecture could be more clearly illuminated there ... Not in basic editing.<br/>Also it''s a candid and a study of the man, so there''s no ''improvement'' needed there.<br/> <br/>Poem:<br/> <br/>Autumnal Retirement<br/> <br/>When old folks'' final days are halcyon<br/>and leave them something, even of this slow<br/>awareness that is all we ever know,<br/>they talk. Old ears enjoy the conversation;<br/>their voices play up in the minor tone.<br/>Their arcane, everyday arpeggio<br/>moves to its own tunes, like the flow<br/>of water in the tide charts of an ocean.<br/> <br/>A cutting edge crests up upon a wave,<br/>a stirring in the rising of the tide<br/>but, where they once behaved heroically,<br/>there is no challenge left to make them brave;<br/>nothing to make, to alter, or decide.<br/>Events occur now, tautologically.</td>', 'Darkness is necessary in a study of light. I''m wondering what could make this better and I''m not getting anywhere with the wondering. I think you could probably lose the strip of light in the foreground and crop to the shadow above it. He cuts a lovely figure and is showing proper respect for what he''s looking at, but if he were St Paul on the road to Damascus he would be looking at the source of the light instead of away from it. Where he''s looking it becomes more a study of the architecture than a study of the light and my wondering asks if a bit of the architecture could be more clearly illuminated there ... Not in basic editing.Also it''s a candid and a study of the man, so there''s no ''improvement'' needed there. Poem: Autumnal Retirement When old folks'' final days are halcyonand leave them something, even of this slowawareness that is all we ever know,they talk. Old ears enjoy the conversation;their voices play up in the minor tone.Their arcane, everyday arpeggiomoves to its own tunes, like the flowof water in the tide charts of an ocean. A cutting edge crests up upon a wave,a stirring in the rising of the tidebut, where they once behaved heroically,there is no challenge left to make them brave;nothing to make, to alter, or decide.Events occur now, tautologically.', '2009-05-01 06:02:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460506, 784213, 57229, '<td valign="top">The processing appears to have been both clever and disastrous :(<br/> <br/>The couple are highlighted, no less, whereas the original suffers for them being indistinct.<br/> <br/>The other thing you did right, of course, was to capture a magnificent candid moment.<br/> <br/>Onward and upward! Basic editing is a drag at times...<br/> <br/>Taking a little longer to look at it is rewarding - another dpc no-no ...<br/> <br/>You''ve definitely done better than most in presenting a moment of private tenderness and joy. Thanks :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-05-01 05:09:45.</i></td>', 'The processing appears to have been both clever and disastrous :( The couple are highlighted, no less, whereas the original suffers for them being indistinct. The other thing you did right, of course, was to capture a magnificent candid moment. Onward and upward! Basic editing is a drag at times... Taking a little longer to look at it is rewarding - another dpc no-no ... You''ve definitely done better than most in presenting a moment of private tenderness and joy. Thanks :)', '2009-05-01 06:07:27.000000', '2009-05-01 06:09:45.000000', 0),
(5460512, 784399, 57229, '<td valign="top">You''re on the front page! Could you hold my hand for a minute? You definitely belong here - this is candid candid candy - well done for catching it.</td>', 'You''re on the front page! Could you hold my hand for a minute? You definitely belong here - this is candid candid candy - well done for catching it.', '2009-05-01 06:13:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460517, 782953, 57229, '<td valign="top">Definitely an ace picture, but hereabouts the genre ''candid'' becomes ''dpc candid'', naturally enough, and unfortunately you dip out there.<br/> <br/>Pig facing the camera would have pushed this higher (not that one has a whole lot of control over that). The inclusion of hairdresser and client reflected in the mirror is great.<br/> <br/>Another one bites the dust, but, you know, pigs are used to that...</td>', 'Definitely an ace picture, but hereabouts the genre ''candid'' becomes ''dpc candid'', naturally enough, and unfortunately you dip out there. Pig facing the camera would have pushed this higher (not that one has a whole lot of control over that). The inclusion of hairdresser and client reflected in the mirror is great. Another one bites the dust, but, you know, pigs are used to that...', '2009-05-01 06:19:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460522, 783868, 57229, '<td valign="top">Voters are pretty definite about what they''re looking for in a challenge like this, I guess. As you now know, a quickly snatched picture of an animal doesn''t fit, whereas a quickly snatched picture of a person does.<br/> <br/>Shame, really, as there''s a whole load of doggy emotion (and lens licking) in this picture. We live and learn. At least you got the picture:)</td>', 'Voters are pretty definite about what they''re looking for in a challenge like this, I guess. As you now know, a quickly snatched picture of an animal doesn''t fit, whereas a quickly snatched picture of a person does. Shame, really, as there''s a whole load of doggy emotion (and lens licking) in this picture. We live and learn. At least you got the picture:)', '2009-05-01 06:24:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460524, 783231, 57229, '<td valign="top">Gaaaahh! Somebody get me out of here! The pictures are climbing off the walls! Gaaaahh!<br/> <br/>Didn''t you read the bit in the handbook where it says that candids are supposed to be sombre meditations on - er - sombre meditations?<br/> <br/>Just another promising candidate standing in the wrong line.<br/> <br/>Shame. Great shot.</td>', 'Gaaaahh! Somebody get me out of here! The pictures are climbing off the walls! Gaaaahh! Didn''t you read the bit in the handbook where it says that candids are supposed to be sombre meditations on - er - sombre meditations? Just another promising candidate standing in the wrong line. Shame. Great shot.', '2009-05-01 06:27:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460528, 784322, 57229, '<td valign="top">Good title - is this the hungover juggling league, by any chance?<br/> <br/>Maybe misses out because it''s as much portrait as it is candid - didn''t hurt the winner though. Did you try b&amp;w?<br/> <br/>Good to see you back. Flame on!</td>', 'Good title - is this the hungover juggling league, by any chance? Maybe misses out because it''s as much portrait as it is candid - didn''t hurt the winner though. Did you try b&w? Good to see you back. Flame on!', '2009-05-01 06:31:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460531, 784376, 57229, '<td valign="top">Just in case you get the feeling not every picture tells a story, this one has a little collection to make up on the shortfall.<br/> <br/>Beautiful pose, beautiful moment - and excellent composition to bring it all together. <br/> <br/>Give yourself a Posthumous green ribbon for this.</td>', 'Just in case you get the feeling not every picture tells a story, this one has a little collection to make up on the shortfall. Beautiful pose, beautiful moment - and excellent composition to bring it all together.  Give yourself a Posthumous green ribbon for this.', '2009-05-01 06:34:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460534, 783464, 57229, '<td valign="top">It''s a personal best! Welcome to the club.<br/> <br/>And you''re supposed to be young and green and ammacher...<br/> <br/>This is a terrific capture of mood and moment - blown out schmown out - you hit the challenge right between the eyes.<br/> <br/>Keep on!</td>', 'It''s a personal best! Welcome to the club. And you''re supposed to be young and green and ammacher... This is a terrific capture of mood and moment - blown out schmown out - you hit the challenge right between the eyes. Keep on!', '2009-05-01 06:37:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460535, 783140, 57229, '<td valign="top">Great picture - sort of needs more than one person in there if you''re going to get the human interaction thing, so maybe that drags it down in the candid stakes.<br/>As a picture/portrait of a blues busker this is top notch.<br/> <br/>ETA: colour distracts - take it from me, I know everything. What?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-05-01 05:40:58.</i></td>', 'Great picture - sort of needs more than one person in there if you''re going to get the human interaction thing, so maybe that drags it down in the candid stakes.As a picture/portrait of a blues busker this is top notch. ETA: colour distracts - take it from me, I know everything. What?', '2009-05-01 06:40:08.000000', '2009-05-01 06:40:58.000000', 0),
(5460539, 782865, 57229, '<td valign="top">Now I know why all those big bad beaten black and blues men sing ''Oh baby''.<br/> <br/>Great take. Please tell me she''s better now?</td>', 'Now I know why all those big bad beaten black and blues men sing ''Oh baby''. Great take. Please tell me she''s better now?', '2009-05-01 06:42:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460541, 783407, 57229, '<td valign="top">Terrific juxtaposition - probably flew right by the dp challenge, but worrafug, eh? I don''t think there''s anything wrong with this at all - could probably use a little rotation, but preferably not at the expense of important details around the edge. <br/>Nice one.</td>', 'Terrific juxtaposition - probably flew right by the dp challenge, but worrafug, eh? I don''t think there''s anything wrong with this at all - could probably use a little rotation, but preferably not at the expense of important details around the edge. Nice one.', '2009-05-01 06:46:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460547, 783796, 57229, '<td valign="top">Poetic mother and child (re)union. Beautifully captured, beautifully presented. I have close to no idea why anything above this scores higher, except maybe for the odd bit of dynamics. Oh, and it''s a lottery.<br/> <br/>Oh, twelfth, damn straight - deserves it, too. Well done, Julianne.</td>', 'Poetic mother and child (re)union. Beautifully captured, beautifully presented. I have close to no idea why anything above this scores higher, except maybe for the odd bit of dynamics. Oh, and it''s a lottery. Oh, twelfth, damn straight - deserves it, too. Well done, Julianne.', '2009-05-01 06:51:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5460548, 782869, 57229, '<td valign="top">You live in a world of your own, don''t you, Jayson? So does the reader here, and the whole composition brings about a meeting of minds outside the canvas.<br/> <br/>I''d echo Posthumous''s comment - it''s a lovely piece of work. Thanks for bringing it.</td>', 'You live in a world of your own, don''t you, Jayson? So does the reader here, and the whole composition brings about a meeting of minds outside the canvas. I''d echo Posthumous''s comment - it''s a lovely piece of work. Thanks for bringing it.', '2009-05-01 06:56:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5462028, 784431, 89230, '<td valign="top">Great Candid shot my friend! I think those that ranked this a 5 or below want to -ok, ill just shut up...</td>', 'Great Candid shot my friend! I think those that ranked this a 5 or below want to -ok, ill just shut up...', '2009-05-01 18:44:17.000000', NULL, 0),
